From a318e634a1483621264231b875a8205d8d47d3e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:19:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] app_server: fix what the static analysis found

- ServerPicture: a copy of a picture that draws another one lost the list
  of nested pictures, and drawing the copy crashed app_server. Both
  BPicture(const BPicture&) and recording a DrawPicture() into another
  picture make such copies. The copy now copies the nested pictures, and
  Play() copes with a picture without any.
- ClientMemoryAllocator: rows of 1 GB overflowed a bitmap's length to 0 (an
  int32 multiplication), and a block of no size, which shares its base with
  its neighbours, was handed out; Free() then merged it with itself and used
  it after freeing it. Such blocks are refused, and the length is computed
  in 64 bits.
- DefaultDecorator: int8 loops over the border width never ended once a bold
  font above about 300 points made the border 128 pixels wide.
- Painter: a gradient without color stops painted stack contents; it now
  paints nothing, as a gradient of TYPE_NONE does.
- Remote drawing: a wheel event whose deltas could not be read was queued
  anyway, and ReadBitmap() ignored its reads' results.

Test: HaikuArmQemu's tools/analysis-fixes/afxtest, picture-clone-nested,
bitmap-length-overflow, gradient-without-stops and decorator-wide-border.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0147-app-server-fix-what-the-static-analysis-found.patch 5702cdd465bf5a24cf4d164d36cc674039e2d982c05ae8d8b51e05efadfd4ff4
